ursors of Alzheimer's disease A4 amyloid protein</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1989</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>126</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2649245</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gingras</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Raught</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Sonenberg</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>eIF4 initiation factors: effectors of mRNA recruitment to ribosomes and regulators of translation</article-title><source>Annu. Rev. Biochem.</source><year>1999</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>913</fpage><lpage>963</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10872469</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Merrick</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cap-dependent and cap-independent translation in eukaryotic systems</article-title><source>Gene</source><year>2004</year><volume>332</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15145049</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gebauer</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Hentze</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular mechanisms of translational control</article-title><source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol.</source><year>2004</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>827</fpage><lpage>835</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15459663</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-